Strategy Design Pattern:
-----------------------
	Strategy pattern defines a family of algorithms ,encapsulates each one,and makes them interchangeble at
runtime.

Select an algorithm behaviour at runtime without modifying the client.

Real Time use case:
-----------------

An e-commerce application supports multple payment methods.

1.Credit Card
2.UPI
3.Paypal

Without Strategy Pattern(Problem)
---------------------------------

class PaymentService
{
 public void pay(String type,double amt)
 {
	if(type.equals("Credit"))
		System.out.prnitln("Payment via credit card:"+amt);
	else if(type.equals("UPI"))
		System.out.prnitln("Payment via credit card:"+UPI);
	else if(type.equals("Paypal"))
		System.out.prnitln("Payment via credit card:"+Paypal);
  }
}

problems:

->voilates open/closed principle
->Hard to extent
->Difficult to test

Using Strategy pattern(Solution)
--------------------------------

interface PaymentStrategy
{
 void pay(double amt);
}

class CreditCardPayment implements PaymentStrategy
{
public void pay(double amt)
{
	System.out.prnitln("amount +" amt+" paid with credit card");
}
}
class UpiPayment implements PaymentStrategy{
{
{
public void pay(double amt)
{
	System.out.prnitln("amount +" amt+" paid with upi");
}
}
class PayPal implements PaymentStrategy{
{
{
public void pay(double amt)
{
	System.out.prnitln("amount +" amt+" paid with PayPal");
}
}

Context class:(strategy)
-------------------------

class PaymentContext
{
	private PaymentStrategy paymentStrategy;
	
	public PaymentContext(PaymentStrategy paymentStrategy)
	{
		this.paymentStrategy=paymentStrategy;
	}
	
	public void executePayment(double amt)
	{
		paymentStrategy.pay(amt);
	}
}


Client code:runtime selection

class Client
{
	public static void main(String args[])
	{
		PaymentContext context=new PaymentContext(new CreditCardPayment());
		context.executePayment(100);
		PaymentContext context=new PaymentContext(new UpiPayment());
		context.executePayment(100);
		PaymentContext context=new PaymentContext(new Paypal());
		context.executePayment(100);
	}
}




